00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:07.269 align:start position:0%
hello today we are going to talk about  stepwise linear discriminant analysis  that is used to find a subset of the  provided features that optimally  separates the classes inherit in the  data  in this procedure a discriminant model  is built iteratively starting with an  empty set of features  lda classification is evaluated on each  feature and the feature resulting in the  highest accuracies added to the optimal  feature set  more and more features are iteratively  added to the set in order of maximum  improvement of accuracy until no  significant improvement is provided by  further features  lda classification can be performed  using a subset of optimal features  without including strongly co-related or  redundant or noisy features which is  known as a forward selection procedure  feature selection is different from  dimensionality reduction although both  methods seek to reduce the number of  attributes in the data set a  dimensionality reduction method does so  by creating new combinations of  attributes feature selection methods  include and exclude attributes present  in the data without changing them  so now to see how this process works  let's run  sw swlda on the tbi info platform  let's use the same input file as for the  other classification pipelines that  include train and test data  you can download the data from lesson  number 15 under transcriptomics on the  portal  you will notice that we have an  additional parameter called niview  it is a user defined parameter for the  stop criterion of feature inclusion  for our expression data which in which  contains expression levels for almost  7000 genes we set this value to 0.005  however for smaller sets higher values  are generally used that is 0.1 or in  some cases lower parameters may be  required when you run this pipeline you  need to play around with the navy  parameter to get it to work correctly  try using point one point zero one point  zero zero one or maybe point zero zero  zero one and compare your outputs  now check the results of the pipeline  we find that it's selected just 17 genes  which are found in discriminant  function.txt output file and if you look  at the confusion matrix we will see the  swa lda achieved 100 accuracy in  predicting the class of test data  to learn more about swlda and how this  algorithm works  and how do you interpret the results  obtained you may visit lesson number 15  under transcriptomics on the honest  logic learn portal
 

